  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Mid and high-level clouds can be seen\nacross northern and central Nevada this morning. Due to the cloud\ncover, temperatures have been fairly steady over most areas with\nreadings in the 40s and 50s. \n\nUpper level ridge circulation can be seen across southern Utah\nthis morning with a weak upper trough over California. The weak\ntrough is expected to slowly push eastward into the forecast area\nlater today. Moisture and instability will be limited, leading to\nroughly a ten to twenty percent probability for showers and\nthunderstorms across the northern portions of I-80, east of a\nWinnemucca to Paradise Valley line. Surface based CAPE values will\nbe around 100 to 150 J/kg in the aforementioned locations. High\ntemperatures will be in the 70s and 80s. The upper trough will\nslowly exit to the east. Models are showing a slightly slower\nprogression and so have kept PoPs between ten and 20 percent\nthrough the early morning hours. Overnight lows will be in the\n40s.\n\nTuesday through Friday night, upper level ridging will rebuild\nwest of the forecast area. This is expected to bring dry and quiet\nweather through the period. Afternoon high temperatures will once\nagain warm to near record to record levels with readings in the\n80s. Overnight lows will be in the 40s. Winds are expected to be\non the light side with occasional breezes to 20 mph.\n\nBy next Saturday models are still hinting at a pattern change \nthat may bring more active, wetter weather back to Nevada in the \nform of a northern stream upper trough, however confidence remains\nvery low as there are still large run to run differences in the \nplacement and strength of the trough in recent model runs. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: Edits were made to the NBM for\nlate this afternoon and evening due to the slower eastward\nprogression of the upper trough through the eastern part of the\nforecast area. Confidence is low at this time regarding the\nisolated showers and thunderstorms later this afternoon across\nnortheast Nevada. High confidence continues for the upper ridge\nrebuilding across the southwestern United States with the return\nof near record to record temperatures Wednesday through the rest\nof the week. There is low confidence with regards to the \npotential of a pattern change as a stronger northern stream \ntrough takes aim at Nevada for the late weekend period.",
